{"type":"finding","severity":"minor","title":"Check the cancellation token before launching a ready successor.","fileName":"crates/paigasus-helikon-core/src/graph.rs","comment":"**Check the cancellation token before launching a ready successor.**

The launch loop starts a successor without checking the cancellation token. Its `RunCompleted` arm pushes ready successors into `ready`, and the top of the loop launches them. The loop yields `AgentUpdated` and calls `nodes[i].1.run(...)` before any cancellation check runs. If a cancelled sibling has more nonterminal events in its stream, the scheduler can consume a completed sibling's `RunCompleted` before the cancelled sibling's end marker. The successor then starts after cancellation, and the end-marker check at lines 303-304 runs only later. A successor that does not check the token itself, such as a custom node with side effects, performs its work.

Check the token in the launch loop, before the successor starts. The check runs only for ready nodes, so a run with no pending work still completes normally.

