{"type":"finding","severity":"minor","title":"Recheck cancellation before each handoff target starts.","fileName":"crates/paigasus-helikon-core/src/agent.rs","comment":"**Recheck cancellation before each handoff target starts.**

Both handoff paths check cancellation, then yield an event (`AgentUpdated` on resume, `HandoffItem` on the live path). A consumer can cancel while that event is delivered. The generator then calls `target_agent.run` without another check, so the target starts with a cancelled token. The target's first turn check returns before any model or tool call, so no model or tool work runs. The start still has visible effects. The live path reports `transferred to <target>` in its transfer results, and both paths fire `OnSubagentStop` for a target that did not run. The existing comment says a token that fired before the handoff must not start it, so this path breaks that stated contract.

Add a check immediately before each startup call. Each check returns with the same cleanup as the existing check above it.

